.TH SDL_memcmp 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_memcmp \- Compare two buffers of memory.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "int SDL_memcmp(const void *s1, const void *s2, size_t len);
.fi
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I s1
the first buffer to compare\[char46] NULL is not permitted!
.TP
.I s2
the second buffer to compare\[char46] NULL is not permitted!
.TP
.I len
the number of bytes to compare between the buffers\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns less than zero if s1 is \(dqless than\(dq s2, greater than zero if s1 is \(dqgreater than\(dq s2, and zero if the buffers match exactly for
.BR len
bytes\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

